kosha dls-pseudoinverse

  -- dls-pseudoinverse: damped least-squares inverse of the Jacobian
  -- solves: delta-theta = J^T (J J^T + lambda I)^{-1} * error
  -- minimum-norm solution for the underdetermined system J * delta-theta = error
  -- lambda (seema) damps the inverse near singularities, preventing blow-up
  -- iterative: krama of Newton-Raphson steps converges to the IK solution

  -- sangati roots: viparita (the act of inversion), seema (lambda = the
  -- damping threshold), krama (iterative steps), viveka (choosing minimum norm)

  "viparita-swarupa krama-siddha"
  "seema-yukta singularity-nirodha"
  "jacobian-viparita norm-seema-yukta"
  "viveka-siddha minimum-norm-phala"
  "ik-siddha joint-space-phala"
  "domain-physics-sthita domain-robotics-sthita"

